# timothyali2: Timothy Ali's rebrand and timothyali.com

The live site at https://www.timothyali.com and the rebrand behind it (positioning, identity, site, social). It is a pixel/type system: bitmap faces on one measured grid, black and white with a theme toggle, yellow as a sparse accent, generated ASCII/dither fields, terminal chrome. No Three.js.

## Where things are

- `docs/decision-log.md`: numbered decisions, newest at the bottom. It is the source of truth when other docs disagree, and the latest explicit direction from Timothy wins over older entries.
- `docs/design-system.md`: tokens, type roles, components and the cell table. Read it before design work.
- `docs/iteration-log.md`, with before/after evidence under `docs/iterations/`.
- `docs/open-questions.md` (undecided items) and `docs/context.md` (the starting point).
- `docs/admin-analytics.md`: the private admin, email sign-in and analytics.
- `tools/review/README.md` (review scripts) and `tools/social/README.md` (favicons and share images).
- Older docs predate the current site: `alternate-v2.md`, the PX-07/PX-08 handoffs, and the city-era `codex-handoff.md`, `implementation-v1.md`, `vector-world.md`, `landing-story.md`, landing copy and storyboards. Check them against the decision log.
- The city version of the landing is saved at `/Users/twocakes/Desktop/PROJECTS/timothyali2-city-v1-2026-09-08`. Don't modify it.
- `../timothyali` is the pre-rebrand checkout of the same repo. Leave it untouched.

## Commands

- `pnpm dev`, `pnpm check`, `pnpm test` (vitest), `pnpm build` (runs `tools/images/derive.mjs` for the WebP derivatives first), `pnpm preview`. Node 22.12 or newer.
- `pnpm seo:check` after a build.
- Share images and icons: `pnpm social:generate`, then `pnpm build` and `pnpm social:verify`. Re-run when titles, selected projects, covers, tools or identity change. They are rendered by the site from the dev-only `/og/[id]` route.
- Toolbox option tables: `tools/toolbox/sync-options.mjs` writes `src/lib/toolbox-options.ts`.
- Review scripts run against `pnpm preview --host 127.0.0.1 --port 4173`.

## Deploy and git

- **Commit and push only on Timothy's word.** Every push to `master` on `origin` (GitHub) is a production deploy through Vercel.
- After pushing `master` to `origin`, push it to `gitlab` too. It is a private mirror and does not deploy.
- The contact form (`src/routes/api/contact/+server.ts`, Resend) and the admin/auth/analytics routes need Vercel's environment. Locally the form reports the relay as unconfigured.
- No root `api/` folder: Vercel's zero-config functions there make every dynamic `/api/...` SvelteKit route answer Vercel's own 404 (0226). Server code goes in `src/routes`.
- Decision numbers 0149 to 0160 belong to the set-aside modernist-v3 work (branch `modernist-v3` and a stash). New decisions continue from the latest number in the log.

## Recording decisions

- Log a decision when Timothy confirms it, not when it is proposed. Label assistant proposals as proposals, and never call a design approved without his confirmation.
- Record his reasons as he gives them. If the reason is unclear, ask; never invent his "why".
- Reversed decisions are not deleted: add a `Superseded by` line and a new entry.
- Log each meaningful iteration in `docs/iteration-log.md`, with before/after evidence under `docs/iterations/`.
- Be a candid peer. Keep direction-setting on the concept and save execution detail for implementation.
- Work directly: Timothy asked for no orchestration skill.

## Privacy

- Résumé sources, cover letters, application material and reviews of his brief are kept privately outside this repo, and résumé and LinkedIn changes are handled there. The only copy here is the phone-free `static/resume/Timothy-Ali-Resume.pdf`.

## Design rules

Details and values are in `docs/design-system.md`. These are the standing rules:

- Every face is a bitmap design sized as cells per em × cell. Font sizes stay on the cell table at the top of `src/app.css`, or the glyph pixels blur. The one exception is the study reading face, IBM Plex Mono (0136, 0137).
- Faces: Jacquard 24 for the wordmark and emphasis, PARC Pixel Bold for uppercase display, PARC Pixel Regular for labels (0078), Jersey 15 for text, Press Start 2P for the readout. PARC Pixel is Timothy's own typeface; it is extended by `tools/fonts/extend-parc-pixel.py`.
- Spacing is in 8px units (0089).
- No rules or borders, and no eyebrow labels anywhere (0047, 0196).
- Black and white with a theme toggle; yellow is a sparse accent (0049).
- Images and video render at their own resolution. Only the generated textures are pixelated (0054).
- Every motion piece has a static version for motion off, no JavaScript and the prerender (0128, 0141).
- Breakpoints are 420, 700, 900 and 1100 (0075).
- Copy has no em dashes. Page titles and quote attributions use "/" (0122). The role is "Product designer" (0172).
- Projects live in `src/lib/work.ts`. Hide one with `hidden: true` and its data stays; every count derives from the visible set. Sonde and Pocketwatch are hidden for now (0219).
- Study facts come from Timothy or recorded sources; the wording around them is marked as the assistant's.
# Design system — as built (PX-14, accepted PX-17, 2026-09-09)

Extracted from the running code in PX-14 on Timothy’s “then do the design system stuff”
(open question Q34). **Accepted by Timothy in decision 0075** (“everything sounds good to me”), including the
three token calls recorded there; the section at the end lists what was proposed and is now the record.
The read-only survey that preceded this is `docs/design-system-inventory.md` — it records
what the code looked like before, including the duplication this pass removed.

The extraction was done under a hard constraint: the site had to render pixel-identically
before and after, except for four deliberate changes. See **Parity** at the end.

## Layers

```
  src/app.css                     the cell table + the import list, nothing else
   ├─ lib/styles/primitives.css   raw values: colour, spacing, cells, faces, motion
   ├─ lib/styles/tokens.css       what a primitive means: paper/fg/accent, surfaces, z, gutter
   ├─ lib/styles/base.css         element defaults, .sr-only, @keyframes blink, the focus
                                  ring, the dither wipes and view transitions, the scrollbar
   ├─ lib/styles/type.css         the named type roles and their ladders
   ├─ lib/styles/chrome.css       sticky header, status strip, global footer
   ├─ lib/styles/layout.css       .site, section, .band, .inner-page
   └─ lib/styles/blocks.css       cursor, ctas, quiet link, page foot, cards, code,
                                  press — the CSS half of the components

  src/lib/tokens.ts               the same primitives for JavaScript
  src/lib/components/*.svelte     markup that chooses class names from blocks.css
  src/routes/*                    structure, and only genuinely one-off sizes
```

Import order is the cascade. A component never carries a scoped `<style>` for a shared
block: the CSS lives in `blocks.css` and the component only decides which classes to emit.
That keeps specificity flat, lets a route position a block it owns, and is why the
refactor could be verified pixel-for-pixel. Routes that need to position an element a
component renders reach it with `:global()` anchored on their own `<main>`.

## Layering (z-index)

```
  --z-skip     99   .skip-link
  --z-nav      50   .nav-chrome (sticky wrapper)
  --z-chrome    2   .site-header, .readout      inside the wrapper
  --z-band      1   a band's content
  --z-band-bg   0   a band's programmatic texture
```

## Tokens

### Layer 1 — primitives (`src/lib/styles/primitives.css`)

| Token | Value | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `--yellow` | `#f2d600` | brand primitive |
| `--ink` | `#181814` | near-black primitive (was `#11110e`; 0171) |
| `--white` | `#efefeb` | off-white primitive (was `#f4f4f0`; 0171) |
| `--yellow-deep` | `#6f6200` | the accent as text on the light ground (5.3:1 on `--white`; 0075, 0171) |
| `--yellow-field` | `#c8ac00` | the accent in a field on the light ground: four oklch lightness steps down (0108) |
| `--u` | `8px` | the spacing unit |
| `--s1 … --s12` | `8 16 24 32 48 64 96px` | the spacing scale; the name is the number of units (`--s4` = 4 × 8). `--s16` and `--cell-text` had no consumer and went in 0210 |
| `--cell-image` | `2px` | gallery column snap unit (0054); figure heights snap to `--u` since 0089 |
| `--cell-texture` | `16px` | one ASCII cell |
| `--face-blackletter` | `'Jacquard 24',serif` | emphasis words, wordmark |
| `--face-display` | `'PARC Pixel Bold Web',sans-serif` | uppercase display (caps-only face; 13.75 cells/em; 0078) |
| `--face-text` | `'Jersey 15',sans-serif` | body and lead |
| `--face-label` | `'PARC Pixel Web',monospace` | labels, nav, buttons (caps-only; 6.25 cells/em; 0078) |
| `--face-mono` | `'Press Start 2P',monospace` | status strip, arrows |
| `--face-root` | `'Jersey 15',ui-monospace,monospace` | the document fallback stack |
| `--tick-cursor` | `1s` | one blink period |
| `--nudge` | `8px` | hover displacement — exactly one cell |
| `--step` / `--step-fast` | `70ms` / `55ms` | one step of a dither wipe; `STEP` / `STEP_FAST` in `tokens.ts` (0100) |

`--cell-image` has no CSS consumer: `rowColumns()` is JavaScript and writes `CELL_IMAGE`
into its `round()` formula. `Picture` and `Clip` floor their heights to `U` (8) through
`src/lib/figure.ts` (0089), so what follows a figure is on the layout grid.

Breakpoints are a comment block in CSS (media queries cannot read custom properties) and
`BP` / `below()` in `tokens.ts` for `matchMedia` and `<source media>` (0210). The four in use are `420 700 900 1100` (0075 folded 1300 into 1100 and moved the phone floor from 380 to 420, shared with the status strip).

### Layer 2 — semantic (`src/lib/styles/tokens.css`)

| Token | Dark (default) | Light | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--paper` | `var(--ink)` | `var(--white)` | page ground |
| `--fg` | `var(--white)` | `var(--ink)` | type / foreground |
| `--accent` | `var(--yellow)` | `var(--yellow)` | fills: cursors, active nav, action blocks |
| `--accent-text` | `var(--yellow)` | `var(--yellow-deep)` | the accent as type: index range, quiet arrows, quiet-link hover, footer toggle state (0075) |
| `--on-accent` | `var(--ink)` | `var(--ink)` | type on accent |
| `--accent-field` | `var(--yellow)` | `var(--yellow-field)` | the accent an ASCII field draws: `.band-bg` sets `--accent-text` to it (0108) |
| `--accent-on-fg` | `var(--yellow-deep)` | `var(--yellow)` | the accent as type on a `--fg` panel — the other ground, the other value; `.who`, `.machine`, `.contact-note`, `.code` set `--accent-text` to it (0106) |
| `--dim` | `.55` | `.65` | secondary-text opacity (a number, not a colour) |
| `--dim-on-fg` | `.65` | `.55` | the dim level on a `.panel` (0210) |
| `--pad-s` / `--pad-m` | `9px 14px 7px 16px` / `17px 14px 15px 16px` | | the label-block paddings: chips and small buttons, rows (0097, named in 0210) |
| `--col-side` | `448px` | | the side column beside Contact's head and Home's invitation |
| `--chrome-height` | `96px` → `104px` ≤700 | | the sticky header and strip: Home's sky starts under it, a held study point sits below it (0210) |
| `--focus-ring` | `2px solid var(--accent-text)` | | the keyboard focus outline |
| `--wipe-in` | `dither-in calc(3 * var(--step)) steps(3) both` | | the three-frame wipe images and themes arrive with |
| `--gutter` | `32px` → `16px` ≤700 | same | page side margin |
| `--header-height` | `64px` | same | default; the layout overrides it inline with the measured height |
| `--surface-card` | `repeating-conic-gradient(color-mix(in srgb,var(--fg) 14%,transparent) 0 25%,transparent 0 50%) 0 0/4px 4px` | | the card dither at rest |
| `--surface-card-hover` | same shape at `26%` and `8px 8px` | | the card dither on hover |
| `--texture-fallback-opacity` | `.35` | | the CSS checker before a canvas has drawn |
| `--field-ink` | `color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 40%, var(--paper))` | | the ASCII field’s colour: recessed, well behind the type (0091) |
| `--tint-fine` / `--tint-rim` / `--tint-major` / `--tint-rule` | `--fg` at `12 / 14 / 22 / 30%` over transparent | | fg tints: admin rules, the card dither and the examples' rims, the admin chart base, the examples' field rules (were `--grid-*`, named after the removed Grid; 0210) |
| `--z-band-bg … --z-skip` | `0 1 2 50 98 99` | | see the layering diagram above |

Theme is applied by `data-theme` on `<html>`, pre-painted by the inline script in
`src/app.html`, mirrored in JS in `+layout.svelte`. `--accent` and `--dim` do not change
with the theme; `--accent-text` does (0075).

### JavaScript (`src/lib/tokens.ts`)

`INK WHITE YELLOW YELLOW_DEEP YELLOW_FIELD rgb()` · `U GALLERY_GAP CELL_IMAGE CELL_TEXTURE` · `BP below()` · `TICK_SLOW=160 TICK_FAST=90`
(Ascii ambient cadence) · `STEP_SLOW=110 STEP=70 STEP_FAST=55` (Decode cadence).

Consumed by `Ascii.svelte` (`cell`, `tick` defaults), `Decode.svelte` (`step` default),
`figure.ts` (the 8px height floor for `Picture` / `Clip`), `+layout.svelte` (the `theme-color`
meta tag) and every Decode/Band call site, so no colour or cadence literal is left in a
route. `src/app.html` keeps its own `#181814` because that script runs before any
stylesheet or module loads; all three places carry a comment naming the other two.

## The typeface build (`tools/fonts/extend-parc-pixel.py`, decision 0078)

PARC Pixel is Timothy's own family from the PARC brand. The site uses its own build, kept in
`tools/fonts/out/` (`parc-pixel.woff2`, `parc-pixel-bold.woff2`, inlined into `base.css`; the
Light and Mono cuts are built too but unused; until 0214 the folder was `static/fonts/`), generated from the untouched originals in `../timothyali/static/parc/`:
seven added glyphs (`[ ] · – — ’ ×`) drawn on each weight's grid, the ampersand redrawn in
every cut (the cut's own 3 mirrored, stubs out the top and bottom), and the Bold rescaled to an
1100-unit em so its cell is exactly 80 units and every advance lands on whole pixels at 41.25,
55, 82.5 and 110. One family name per weight (`PARC Pixel Web`, `PARC Pixel Bold Web`) because
each weight has its own cells-per-em. Rebuild with a venv that has `fonttools` and `brotli`.
Fractional font sizes (12.5, 41.25, 27.5) are on the table: the cell is what has to be whole.

## The cell table

Every face is a bitmap design; its em is a known number of cells, so
`font-size = cells per em × cell size` and glyph pixels land on device pixels. The table
lives at the top of `src/app.css` and is the reason font sizes are **not** tokens: a token
would hide the arithmetic.

| face | cells/em | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 6 | 8 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Jacquard 24 | 43 | 43 | 86 | 129 | 172 | 258 | 344 |
| PARC Pixel Bold | 13.75 | — | 27.5 | 41.25 | 55 | 82.5 | 110 |
| Jersey 15 | 27 | 27 | 54 | | | | |
| PARC Pixel | 6.25 | — | 12.5 | 18.75 | 25 | 37.5 | 50 |
| Press Start 2P | 8 | 8 | 16 | 24 | 32 | | |

## Type roles (`src/lib/styles/type.css`)

| Role | Face | Ladder |
|---|---|---|
| `.blackletter` | Jacquard 24 | family only, `line-height:1` |
| `.display-xl` | — (always worn with `.blackletter`) | **258/264 → 172/176 (≤1100) → 129/136 (≤700) → 86/88 (≤420)**, `display:block` |
| `.display` | PARC Pixel Bold | 55/56 → 41.25/48 (≤700), uppercase (cell 4 → 3) |
| `.display-s` | PARC Pixel Bold | 41.25/48 → 27.5/32 (≤700), uppercase (cell 3 → 2) |
| `.lead` | Jersey 15 | 54/64 → 27/32 (≤700); the study's single lead paragraph is 27/40 at every width, capped at 64ch (0123) |
| `.body` | Jersey 15 | 27/32; the study's reading paragraphs (`.paras`) 27/40 in a 64ch column (PX-43) |
| `.lbl` | PARC Pixel | 12.5/16, uppercase (cell 2) |
| `.mono` | Press Start 2P | 16/16, uppercase, nowrap |
| `.read` | IBM Plex Mono (`--face-read`, `@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono`, preloaded on study pages) | 18/32 at every width, smoothed; the case-study reading text only: lead, meta values, paragraphs, list items (0136, 0137). The one face that is not a bitmap |
| `.dim` | — | `opacity:var(--dim)` |

`.display-xl` replaces the three route-local `.xl` copies (Home, Work, Contact).
`.display-l` (123px, never used in any route) is retired.

Route-local sizes that stayed route-local because they are genuinely one-off: `.hero-name`
(344 / 258 ≤1100 / 129 ≤700), the study `.title` (PARC Pixel Bold 110 / 82.5 ≤1100 / 55 ≤900 / 41.25 ≤700 plus the
JS-measured `.small` step-down), Home’s `.para` / `.words` / `.w` and
`.work-statement .blackletter`. A card title steps down to 27.5 and 20.625 when its longest
word is wider than the card (`fitTitles`, `$lib/fit`, one size per grid).

