## 0145 — SEO audit and optimisation pass

- **Date:** 2026-10-02
- **Direction:** Timothy: “i want to set up a thorough SEO audit. get things nice and optimized.”
- **Audit.** Every prerendered page already had a unique title and description, one `h1`, alt text and dimensions on every image, canonical, Open Graph and Twitter tags, JSON-LD, a sitemap and a 404 with `noindex` (0086); Lighthouse SEO scored 100 on every page tested and accessibility 100. What was left was performance and depth: 41MB of PNG/JPEG referenced with no modern format or responsive sizes (the Work page's LCP was 5.4s on mobile, its first cover a 2880px PNG for a 380px slot; Home's main thread was blocked 510ms drawing three textures at once), every static file served with `max-age=0`, no security headers, a 200 at `/index.html`, the Work description at 50 characters and the tool pages' at 60–71, structured data without a page node, and the sitemap carrying no images. Semrush's API had no units left, so the audit is first-hand: a static pass over the build, live header checks, and Lighthouse (`docs/iterations/pixel-v2/59-seo-audit/`).
- **Decision (PX-59).** (1) Responsive WebP: `tools/images/derive.mjs` (sharp) writes `name.<w>.webp` beside every raster under `static/work` and `static/toolbox` at 640/1000/1600/2400 capped at the master's width (a `@2x` is the master where one exists; UI screens at quality 90, photographs at 82), and a manifest `src/lib/images.json`; the derivatives are git-ignored and made by `pnpm build`, the manifest is committed. `Picture` and the Home wheel's card put a `<source type="image/webp" srcset sizes>` in front of the original, which stays the fallback at its own resolution (0054 holds); eager images carry `fetchpriority="high"`; the Work rows and study galleries state their real slot widths. (2) `vercel.json`: a week's `Cache-Control` with a month's stale-while-revalidate on images, video, fonts and icons, a day on the résumé; `nosniff`, `Referrer-Policy`, `X-Frame-Options`, `Permissions-Policy` on every response; `/index.html` → `/`. (3) `Ascii` waits to draw a field that mounts off screen until it comes within 64px (the on-screen check at mount is synchronous, so nothing visible changes). (4) `seo.ts`: every page is a `WebPage` (Work a `CollectionPage`, Contact a `ContactPage`) that is part of the `WebSite`, with its share image and breadcrumb; the Person carries the studio email; each study's `CreativeWork` is the page's main entity with an `ImageObject`, keywords from its tools, and its place in the Work collection; Toolbox's `SoftwareApplication` gains a free offer, download URL, screenshot and help page. (5) The sitemap lists each study's cover and screens and each tool page's screenshot as image entries (121 images). (6) Descriptions: Work names the selected four (156 characters); a tool page adds “Part of Toolbox, Timothy Ali’s free desktop app for macOS and Linux.” Both the page tag and the share tags read one source in `social.ts`. (7) `tools/review/seo.mjs` (`pnpm seo:check`) is the audit as a regression check over the build, and `derive.mjs --check` catches stale derivatives.
- **Assistant proposals inside it:** the two description wordings and the word “free” (the builds are public GitHub releases with no purchase anywhere; also stated as the schema offer), the cache lifetimes, the WebP ladder and qualities, and the texture deferral.
- **Measured (local, same server for both, mobile):** Home 1195KB → 493KB and LCP 5.9s → 4.3s; Work 1146KB → 444KB, LCP 7.6s → 4.0s; PARC 697KB → 506KB; Sonde 513KB → 448KB (its screens were already phone crops). Production numbers come after a deploy.
- **Not done, and outside the repo:** the apex `timothyali.com` → `www` redirect is a 307 from Vercel's domain settings and should be 308 (dashboard, not code); the hosted résumé PDF says “Chromium” as its author (set in the private build); the sitemap has not been resubmitted to Search Console; no `lastmod` (0086 stands).
- **Status:** implemented and verified (`pnpm check` 0/0, 24 tests, build, `social:verify`, `seo:check` PASS, Home and Sonde checked in the browser at desktop and phone widths); uncommitted, awaiting Timothy's word.

